@startuml
skinparam componentStyle rectangle

rectangle "UI Thread" {
    component "MainWindow" as MainWindow
    component "TaskManager" as TaskManager
    component "TaskRegistry" as TaskRegistry
    component "TaskRuntimeStore" as TaskRuntimeStore
    component "TaskPresenter" as TaskPresenter
    component "TaskView" as TaskView
}

rectangle "Worker Thread" {
    component "QtTaskRunner" as QtTaskRunner
    component "QtProgressReporter" as QtProgressReporter
    component "DomainTask" as DomainTask
}

MainWindow --> TaskManager : composition root
TaskManager --> TaskRegistry : resolve task definition
TaskManager --> TaskRuntimeStore : keep runtime state
TaskManager --> TaskPresenter : bind view behavior
TaskManager --> TaskView : create configured view

TaskPresenter --> TaskView : user interaction + UI state
TaskPresenter --> TaskRuntimeStore : runtime updates
TaskPresenter --> QtTaskRunner : create per task start

QtTaskRunner --> DomainTask : execute()
QtTaskRunner --> QtProgressReporter : progress/cancel bridge
QtProgressReporter --> TaskPresenter : error/finished via queued signal
QtProgressReporter --> TaskView : progress/message via presenter callbacks

note right of TaskManager
Acts as a framework coordinator,
not as domain logic.
end note

note bottom of Worker Thread
Worker side never touches QWidget directly.
end note
@enduml
